{"jacobs":{"section":"4.6","pages":"163 to 168","references":[{"section":"4.6","pages":[163,168]}],"relationship":""},"key":"U04-L11","slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Why SSA Fails","items":[],"html":"<h2>Why SSA Fails</h2><p>I can give a counterexample showing SSA is not a congruence test.</p>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Why SSA Fails","kind":"cover","jacobs":{"section":"4.6","pages":"163 to 168","references":[{"section":"4.6","pages":[163,168]}],"relationship":""},"target":"I can give a counterexample showing SSA is not a congruence test.","stds":"","cover":"geometry/covers/u04.svg"}},{"n":2,"title":"Get started","items":[],"html":"<p>Swinging door: fix side AB and the angle at A, then swing a fixed-length 'door' BC from B. It hits the ray in two places.</p><ul><li>I can build two different triangles from the same SSA data with compass and ruler.</li><li>I can explain why SSA is not a congruence test even when the sides are long.</li></ul>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Get started","kind":"text","v2":true,"body":"<p>Swinging door: fix side AB and the angle at A, then swing a fixed-length 'door' BC from B. It hits the ray in two places.</p><ul><li>I can build two different triangles from the same SSA data with compass and ruler.</li><li>I can explain why SSA is not a congruence test even when the sides are long.</li></ul>"}},{"n":3,"title":"The big idea","items":[],"html":"<p>SSA can give two, one or no triangles, so it is not a test.</p>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"The big idea","kind":"text","v2":true,"body":"<p>SSA can give two, one or no triangles, so it is not a test.</p>"}},{"n":4,"title":"Worked example","items":[],"html":"<p>Swinging door: one SSA recipe, two triangles (student version of Euclid&#39;s example).</p><details><summary>Read the worked steps</summary><table><tr><th>Step</th><th>Reason</th></tr><tr><td>Draw a ray from A. Mark B above it so that AB = 5 and the angle at A is fixed.</td><td>These are the given side and angle.</td></tr><tr><td>Open the compass to the given length BC. Put the point on B and swing an arc.</td><td>Every point on the arc is that distance from B.</td></tr><tr><td>The arc hits the ray twice. Call the points C1 and C2.</td><td>A circle can cross a line in two places.</td></tr><tr><td>Triangles ABC1 and ABC2 have the same angle A, the same AB, and the same BC.</td><td>Same ray, same side, same compass setting.</td></tr><tr><td>But AC1 = 3 and AC2 = 5, so the triangles are not congruent.</td><td>Their third sides are different.</td></tr><tr><td>So SSA is not a congruence test.</td><td>One counterexample is enough.</td></tr></table></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Worked example","kind":"worked-example","prompt":"Swinging door: one SSA recipe, two triangles (student version of Euclid's example).","steps":[{"step":"Draw a ray from A. Mark B above it so that AB = 5 and the angle at A is fixed.","reason":"These are the given side and angle."},{"step":"Open the compass to the given length BC. Put the point on B and swing an arc.","reason":"Every point on the arc is that distance from B."},{"step":"The arc hits the ray twice. Call the points C1 and C2.","reason":"A circle can cross a line in two places."},{"step":"Triangles ABC1 and ABC2 have the same angle A, the same AB, and the same BC.","reason":"Same ray, same side, same compass setting."},{"step":"But AC1 = 3 and AC2 = 5, so the triangles are not congruent.","reason":"Their third sides are different."},{"step":"So SSA is not a congruence test.","reason":"One counterexample is enough."}],"optional":false,"figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":5,"title":"Worked example","items":[],"html":"<p>Bigger doesn&#39;t fix it (student version).</p><details><summary>Read the worked steps</summary><table><tr><th>Step</th><th>Reason</th></tr><tr><td>Draw the same picture twice as big. AB is now 10, and the angle at A doesn&#39;t change.</td><td>The rays from A point the same way, so angle A is the same.</td></tr><tr><td>The compass arc from B still hits the ray twice.</td><td>Same picture, just larger.</td></tr><tr><td>The two third sides are still different.</td><td>So long sides don&#39;t rescue SSA.</td></tr></table></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Worked example","kind":"worked-example","prompt":"Bigger doesn't fix it (student version).","steps":[{"step":"Draw the same picture twice as big. AB is now 10, and the angle at A doesn't change.","reason":"The rays from A point the same way, so angle A is the same."},{"step":"The compass arc from B still hits the ray twice.","reason":"Same picture, just larger."},{"step":"The two third sides are still different.","reason":"So long sides don't rescue SSA."}],"optional":false,"figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":6,"title":"Try it","items":[],"html":"<p>Use the controls. A drawing suggests a result; it is not a proof.</p>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Try it","kind":"gx","gx":"u04.ssa"}},{"n":7,"title":"Common mistake","items":[],"html":"<p>Jordan says longer sides make SSA a congruence test.</p><p>Try it on paper first, then reveal.</p><details><summary>Find and fix the error</summary><p>SSA is not a universal congruence test. In the special pictured case, the circle is tangent to the supporting line at a point C strictly beyond A on the ray, and BC is perpendicular to the line. Then ABC is one nondegenerate (real, not flat) right triangle. A single intersection on a ray is not always a tangency.</p></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Common mistake","kind":"common-mistake","prompt":"Jordan says longer sides make SSA a congruence test.","correction":"<p>SSA is not a universal congruence test. In the special pictured case, the circle is tangent to the supporting line at a point C strictly beyond A on the ray, and BC is perpendicular to the line. Then ABC is one nondegenerate (real, not flat) right triangle. A single intersection on a ray is not always a tangency.</p>","figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":8,"title":"Practice 1","items":[],"html":"<p>In Worked example 1, which angle is included between AB and BC?</p><p>Try it on paper first, then reveal.</p><details><summary>Reveal solution</summary><p>Angle ABC, not angle BAC.</p><details><summary>Reveal second check</summary><p>The two sides share the point B.</p></details></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Practice 1","kind":"practice","prompt":"In Worked example 1, which angle is included between AB and BC?","solution":"Angle ABC, not angle BAC.","check":"The two sides share the point B.","figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":9,"title":"Practice 2","items":[],"html":"<p>Do the two triangles in Worked example 1 have the same angle A?</p><p>Try it on paper first, then reveal.</p><details><summary>Reveal solution</summary><p>Yes. Both use ray AB and the same ray from A.</p><details><summary>Reveal second check</summary><p>The two rays are exactly the same in both triangles.</p></details></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Practice 2","kind":"practice","prompt":"Do the two triangles in Worked example 1 have the same angle A?","solution":"Yes. Both use ray AB and the same ray from A.","check":"The two rays are exactly the same in both triangles.","figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":10,"title":"Practice 3","items":[],"html":"<p>Why does AC1 = 3 and AC2 = 5 prove the triangles are not congruent?</p><p>Try it on paper first, then reveal.</p><details><summary>Reveal solution</summary><p>The other two sides match, but the third sides differ.</p><details><summary>Reveal second check</summary><p>Call the shared compass length r. The perimeters are 3 + r + 5 = 8 + r and 5 + r + 5 = 10 + r. They differ, so even changing the vertex matching cannot make the triangles congruent.</p></details></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Practice 3","kind":"practice","prompt":"Why does AC1 = 3 and AC2 = 5 prove the triangles are not congruent?","solution":"The other two sides match, but the third sides differ.","check":"Call the shared compass length r. The perimeters are 3 + r + 5 = 8 + r and 5 + r + 5 = 10 + r. They differ, so even changing the vertex matching cannot make the triangles congruent.","figure":{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 400\"><circle cx=\"210.4647723677454\" cy=\"185.00000000000003\" r=\"114.99999999999997\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M311.5633516435545,298.0985792758091L319.5633516435545,294.0985792758091L311.5633516435545,290.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M65,294.0985792758091L210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L174.09857927580907,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M210.4647723677454,185.00000000000003L246.83096545968175,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"284.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">A</text><text x=\"226.4647723677454\" y=\"173.00000000000003\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">B</text><text x=\"162.09857927580907\" y=\"318.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C1</text><text x=\"260.83096545968175\" y=\"282.0985792758091\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">C2</text><path d=\"M187.53825933152467,237.96815080782036L197.0250923120298,241.13042846798876\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M223.904452423461,241.13042846798876L233.39128540396615,237.96815080782036\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M84.2,279.6985792758091Q65,294.0985792758091 89,294.0985792758091\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"97.7323861838727\" y=\"239.54928963790456\" fill=\"black\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AB = 5</text><path d=\"M65,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091M65,322.0985792758091H174.09857927580907M174.09857927580907,318.0985792758091V326.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.54928963790454\" y=\"342.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC1 = 3</text><path d=\"M65,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091M65,359.0985792758091H246.83096545968175M246.83096545968175,355.0985792758091V363.0985792758091\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"155.91548272984087\" y=\"379.0985792758091\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"serif\" font-size=\"32\">AC2 = 5</text></svg>","src":null,"alt":"One ray from A, one circle at B and two possible triangles: AB = 5, AC1 = 3, AC2 = 5."}}},{"n":11,"title":"Check yourself","items":[],"html":"<p>What condition gives one right triangle in the swinging-door picture?</p><p>Try it on paper first, then reveal.</p><details><summary>Reveal solution</summary><p>The circle is tangent at the perpendicular foot from B, and that foot lies strictly past A on the ray. A single ray crossing is not always a tangency.</p><details><summary>Reveal second check</summary><p>Name the givens and the theorem or definition used.</p></details></details>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Check yourself","kind":"practice","prompt":"What condition gives one right triangle in the swinging-door picture?","solution":"The circle is tangent at the perpendicular foot from B, and that foot lies strictly past A on the ray. A single ray crossing is not always a tangency.","check":"Name the givens and the theorem or definition used.","figure":{"svg":null,"alt":""}}},{"n":12,"title":"Exit ticket","items":[],"html":"<ol><li>Sketch SSA data that makes two triangles.</li><li>Does making every length bigger fix SSA? Why?</li><li>What's confusing?</li></ol>","geo":{"tag":"GEOMETRY · UNIT 4 · LESSON 4.11","title":"Exit ticket","kind":"exit-ticket","body":"<ol><li>Sketch SSA data that makes two triangles.</li><li>Does making every length bigger fix SSA? Why?</li><li>What's confusing?</li></ol>"}}]}
